language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ csplib_002_template_design: an Essence' model from DCP Rosetta.
$
$ Template design: a colour printing firm makes several design variations of a product on mother sheets of board, each sheet made from a template. Every template has a given number of slots, and every slot of a template is filled with one copy of a variation. Decide which variations, and how many copies of each, go on each template, and how many sheets to make from each template. Each template yields between 1 sheet and as many sheets as the largest demand. The sheets made must meet at least the demand of every variation, and the total number of sheets made is to be minimized.
$
$ Save this file as model.eprime. Download `csplib_002_template_design.json` and `dcp_convert_essence.py` from the
$ problem's page:
$   https://dcp-bench.github.io/DCP-Rosetta/problems/csplib_002_template_design.html
$ Convert the instances once, then run the first one with Savile Row 1.11 (it needs Java); the
$ solution is written to `csplib_002_template_design_1.param.solution`:
$   python dcp_convert_essence.py csplib_002_template_design.json
$   savilerow model.eprime csplib_002_template_design_1.param -run-solver

$ n_var: the number of design variations (indices 1-based)
given n_var : int(1..)
$ demand[v]: the number of copies of variation v that must be printed, indices 1-based
given demand : matrix indexed by [int(1..n_var)] of int(0..)
$ n_templates: the number of templates
given n_templates : int(1..)
$ n_slots: the number of slots on each template
given n_slots : int(1..)

$ layout[t,v]: the number of copies of variation v on template t
find layout : matrix indexed by [int(1..n_templates), int(1..n_var)] of int(0..n_slots)
$ production[t]: the number of sheets printed from template t
find production : matrix indexed by [int(1..n_templates)] of int(1..sum(demand))

minimising sum t : int(1..n_templates) . production[t]
such that
$ every slot of each template is filled
forAll t : int(1..n_templates) . (sum v : int(1..n_var) . layout[t,v]) = n_slots,
$ each template prints between 1 sheet and as many sheets as the largest demand
forAll t : int(1..n_templates) . production[t] <= max(demand),
$ the sheets printed meet the demand of every variation
forAll v : int(1..n_var) . (sum t : int(1..n_templates) . production[t] * layout[t,v]) >= demand[v]
